outputs.L1:
The invention relates to a production station for producing at least one layered bed, and in particular a plurality of layered beds, of a magnetocaloric material. The production station comprises a framework and the following components arranged thereon:

- a material receptacle configured to receive a particulate magnetocaloric material;
- a dosing plate having at least one intake opening configured to receive magnetocaloric material for one layer of the layered bed;
- at least one reservoir positioned below the at least one intake opening and configured to receive one or more layers of the particulate magnetocaloric material; and
- a shutter plate arranged between the reservoir and the dosing plate.

The shutter plate is switchable by movement relative to the dosing plate and is arranged and configured to activate at least a filling mode. In the filling mode, the at least one reservoir is filled with particulate magnetocaloric material for the one layer of the layered bed through switching control of the shutter plate.

counterfactuals.output:
1. **A production station for forming a layered bed of particulate magnetocaloric material, the production station comprising:**

a receptacle having a bed-forming cavity configured to receive a plurality of layers of particulate magnetocaloric material;

a dosing plate disposed above the receptacle and including a plurality of dosing openings arranged over the bed-forming cavity;

a reservoir configured to supply the particulate magnetocaloric material to the dosing openings;

a shutter plate disposed between the dosing plate and the receptacle and movable relative to the dosing plate between a closed position, in which the shutter plate obstructs communication between the dosing openings and the bed-forming cavity, and an open position, in which respective passage openings of the shutter plate align with the dosing openings to permit metered quantities of the particulate magnetocaloric material to pass into the bed-forming cavity; and

an actuator configured to move the shutter plate between the closed position and the open position,

wherein the dosing plate, the shutter plate, and the receptacle are arranged such that repeated movement of the shutter plate between the closed position and the open position deposits successive, discrete layers of the particulate magnetocaloric material in the bed-forming cavity to form the layered bed.
